[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791314916","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105217#issuecomment-2791314916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105217","id":2791314916,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mYBXk","user":{"login":"JoNax97","id":10124534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10124534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97","html_url":"https://github.com/JoNax97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T01:23:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T01:23:53Z","body":"If I understand the code correctly, the way the ids work is that each peer assigns an id to their own version of the node and broadcasts it to all other peers right? So each peer knows how to refer to a node to any other peer, but the ids themselves are not the same for all peers.\r\n\r\nIf this is to be used alongside RPCs, it means users cannot call rpc() once, but must instead iterate over all peers, get their own id, and then call rpc_id() for each peer individually.\r\n\r\nThis can be alleviated by having the engine do the conversion internally when a node is detected in the rpc parameters. I guess it might still incur some performance penalty, as the payload must be re-encoded for each peer separately.\r\n\r\nMaybe the system can be reworked so that the peer that has authority over the node assigns the network id for all other peers? That would be way outside the scope of this PR in any case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791314916/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791623169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105217#issuecomment-2791623169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105217","id":2791623169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mZMoB","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T05:46:16Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T05:46:16Z","body":"> users cannot call rpc() once, but must instead iterate over all peers, get their own id, and then call rpc_id() for each peer individually.\r\n\r\nThis seems like a significant drawback.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https