"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2798938864","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105217#issuecomment-2798938864","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105217","id":2798938864,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m1Grw","user":{"login":"elementbound","id":4706096,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDYwOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4706096?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound","html_url":"https://github.com/elementbound","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elementbound/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-12T18:25:14Z","updated_at":"2025-04-12T18:25:14Z","body":"@JoNax97 I think the issue of having to re-encode the packet for every target can be avoided, by using the locally assigned ID when talking to peers that know about it, and using the node path for peers that don't. This way, you get at most two buffers to encode, instead of one per peer. \r\n\r\nIf memory serves right, Godot does this under the hood too for RPCs. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2798938864/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0